  "unresolved_gaps": [
    "Frozen OeisA135508.conjecture is still sorry.",
    "Remaining class: primes p ≡ 1 (mod 3) with p-2 composite, lpf(p-2) ≥ 113, and that least factor not a larger twin.",
    "conjecture_of_square_window reduces the frozen type to q | x(q(q+2)-1) for every prime q ≥ 5. That hypothesis is not proved.",
    "conjecture_of_C1 is Cloitre Cor. 6.6 as an implication from C1. C1 is not proved.",
    "conjecture_of_minFac_entered reduces remaining McEachen to q | x(q(q+2)-1) for q = lpf(p-2).",
    "exists_prime_index_injector proves an unbounded prime injector via Dirichlet; it does not prove r ≤ q(q+2)-1.",
    "q_dvd_x_window_of_no_small_factor: k ≡ 5 (mod 6), k ≤ q, and no prime p < q dividing kq-2, implies the window. Existence of such k is not proved. A first-order union bound is negative.",
    "conjecture_of_paired_injectors is a proper subfamily (5q-2, 7q-2, 5s-2, or 7s-2 prime). Scan of remaining p<200000: 332 of 466 covered; 134 uncovered by that pairing.",
    "leftover_injectors.py: all 466 leftover p<200000 have some factor injector k ≤ (p-2)/r. Zero McEachen-window gaps in that range. Not a proof.",
    "conjecture_of_add_two_overlap needs gcd(q+2, p-2)>1. Only 5 of those 466 leftover primes.",
    "If n≥9 and 3∣a n then 2187∣n+1. If n≥10 and 3∣a n then 6561∣n+1. If n≥12 and 3∣a n then 19683∣n+1. Those are not McEachen.",
    "Need a prime r = kq-2 with r ≤ q(q+2)-1. For q ≡ 2 (mod 3) the candidates are k ≡ 5 (mod 6).",
    "Dirichlet, Linnik L=5, and the usual GRH bound do not give r ≤ q(q+2)-1. Finite injector checks are not a proof.",
    "Miller-Rabin to q ≤ 1000000 found no window failures (worst k=257 at q=40973). Not a proof.",
    "Cloitre C1 and Cor. 6.6 are not an unconditional solution."
  ],
